            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Clara Barton: Early Life</strong><br>\nClara Barton was born on December 25, 1821, in Massachusetts. Growing up, she was shy and timid but found a passion for helping others at a young age. When her brother was injured, Clara cared for him for two years, which sparked her interest in nursing. Her early education was provided by her older siblings, and she later became a teacher herself, opening a free public school in New Jersey.</p>\n\n<p><strong>The Civil War and Nursing</strong><br>\nDuring the Civil War, Clara Barton sought to help the soldiers in any way she could. She began by collecting supplies for the Union Army but soon moved to the front lines. Barton risked her life to bring food, supplies, and personal aid to troops in the field. Her bravery and dedication earned her the nickname \"Angel of the Battlefield.\"</p>\n\n<p><strong>Post-War Efforts and Advocacy</strong><br>\nAfter the war, Clara Barton worked at the Office of Missing Soldiers, helping to identify and bury the dead. She also lectured about her war experiences, advocating for the recognition of the International Red Cross in the United States. Barton's efforts were instrumental in the eventual establishment of the American Red Cross.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
